class_name LevelData
## Platformer stage definitions. Each map is ASCII, one character per 16x16 tile.
##
## Legend:
##   #  ground (grass on top when open above)    %  stone (mossy top when open above)
##   =  one-way wooden plank (jump up through it, Down+Jump drops through)
##   |  climbable vine        +  plank with a vine running through it
##   c  dark cave background (passable)          .  empty
##   ^  thorns (hurt, then respawn on safe ground)
##   w  twig: trips you unless you jump over it or crawl across
##   <  >  seed pod shooting left / right        v  acorn dropper (drops from above)
##   o  item pickup   — uses "items" in order, left to right
##   ?  tutorial hint zone (the whole column) — uses "hints" in order, left to right
##   !  readable sign — uses "signs" in order, left to right
##   E  thornling (touch = battle)               D  training dummy (combat tutorial)
##   k  bench (heal + save)    G  goal flag (stage clear)    B  boss gate (boss fight)
##   P  player start
## Text may use {action} tokens (e.g. {jump}) which become the player's button labels.

